            <ArticleTitle>[CHOICE OF THE TREATMENT TACTICS IN PATIENTS, SUFFERING POSTOPERATIVE HERNIA OF ANTERIOR ABDOMINAL WALL WITH CONCOMITANT MORBID OBESITY].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Experience of treatment of 73 patients, suffering postoperative hernia of anterior abdominal wall with concomitant obesity, was presented. In 31 (42.5%) of them in a period of reduction and stabilization of a body mass the allohernioplasty as a second stage after bariatric operation was done, and in 9 (42.5%)--simultant bariatric operations with hernioplasty and dermatolipectomy. During a follow-up period after bariatric operation and hernioplasty the hernia recurrence have occurred in 3 (9.1%) patients, after hernioplasty--in 11 (33.3%), witnessing high efficacy of staged treatment in such patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
